  "changed_since_previous": "Switched from widening existing int parameters to parsing `count` and `skip` as `uint32_t` via `self.Arg`. Removed manual negative value checks in favor of RPC schema validation (changing the error code on negative inputs from RPC_INVALID_PARAMETER (-8) to RPC_INVALID_REQUEST (-1)), and refactored clamping logic using `std::min` with `size_t`.",
  "card": "Fixes a node crash in the listtransactions wallet RPC when count + skip exceeds INT_MAX. On unpatched nodes, supplying large non-negative integer arguments triggers a signed integer overflow that passes invalid reverse iterator offsets to UniValue, crashing bitcoind. The PR switches argument parsing to uint32_t via self.Arg, computes their limit in uint64_t, and adds regression tests for boundary values.",
